WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.310 --> 00:00:03.129
WHEN THE RIGHT SONG BECOMES
A PART OF THE RIGHT MOVIE,

00:00:03.129 --> 00:00:04.810
IT STAYS WITH US FOREVER.

00:00:04.810 --> 00:00:07.350
YOU CAN NEVER HEAR THAT SONG
AGAIN WITHOUT THINKING

00:00:07.350 --> 00:00:08.920
ABOUT ITS MOVIE PARTNER.

00:00:08.920 --> 00:00:11.690
THAT IS THE POWER OF MUSIC.

00:00:11.690 --> 00:00:13.480
ALTHOUGH MOST OF THE NOMINEES
WERE ABLE TO MAKE IT TO

00:00:13.480 --> 00:00:16.170
LOS ANGELES, THERE ARE A PAIR
JOINING US FROM SWEDEN.

00:00:16.170 --> 00:00:18.859
SO, HERE ARE THE NOMINEES
FOR BEST SONG.

00:00:33.669 --> 00:00:35.537
AND THE OSCAR GOES TO --

00:00:36.894 --> 00:00:40.686
H.E.R., DERNST EMILE II,
AND TIARA THOMAS

00:00:40.686 --> 00:00:43.293
"FIGHT FOR YOU" FROM "JUDAS AND
THE BLACK MESSIAH”

00:00:43.293 --> 00:00:46.313
[ CHEERS AND APPLAUSE ]

00:01:05.544 --> 00:01:06.922
OH MY GOD.

00:01:07.574 --> 00:01:10.109
I DID NOT EXPECT
TO WIN THIS AWARD.

00:01:10.109 --> 00:01:13.610
I AM SO, SO, SO, SO GRATEFUL.

00:01:13.610 --> 00:01:14.324
NOT ONLY TO WIN,

00:01:14.324 --> 00:01:18.166
BUT TO BE A PART OF SUCH
AN IMPORTANT, IMPORTANT STORY.

00:01:18.166 --> 00:01:19.780
SO THANK YOU SO MUCH.

00:01:19.780 --> 00:01:21.200
THANK YOU TO THE ACADEMY.

00:01:21.200 --> 00:01:23.990
I’VE ALWAYS WANTED 
TO SAY THAT.

00:01:23.990 --> 00:01:24.619
AND OF COURSE,

00:01:24.619 --> 00:01:26.700
MY COLLABORATORS, D’MILE
AND TIARA THOMAS,

00:01:26.700 --> 00:01:29.560
THIS SONG WOULDN’T BE
WHAT IT WAS WITHOUT THEM.

00:01:32.340 --> 00:01:34.829
OF COURSE, I HAVE TO
THANK GOD FOR GIVING US

00:01:34.829 --> 00:01:38.409
THESE GIFTS AND MY PARENTS,
MY BEAUTIFUL MOTHER WHO’S

00:01:38.409 --> 00:01:40.610
HERE WITH ME TODAY
AND MY FATHER AT HOME.

00:01:40.610 --> 00:01:43.759
ALL THOSE DAYS OF LISTENING
TO SLY AND THE FAMILY STONE,

00:01:43.759 --> 00:01:46.139
AND CURTIS MAYFIELD AND MARVIN
GAYE, THEY REALLY PAID OFF.

00:01:46.139 --> 00:01:48.474
SO THANK YOU, DAD.

00:01:50.530 --> 00:01:52.196
THANK YOU SO MUCH TO ARCHIE

00:01:52.196 --> 00:01:55.109
AND SHAKA KING AND EVERYBODY
THAT WAS INVOLVED IN THIS MOVIE

00:01:55.109 --> 00:01:58.569
AND GAVE ME THE CALL AND
GAVE US THE CALL TO DO THIS RECORD.

00:01:58.569 --> 00:02:01.280
I’M SO, SO GRATEFUL.

00:02:01.280 --> 00:02:02.490
I JUST WANT TO SAY THIS.

00:02:02.490 --> 00:02:07.270
YOU KNOW MUSICIANS, FILMMAKERS,
I BELIEVE WE HAVE AN OPPORTUNITY

00:02:07.270 --> 00:02:11.720
AND A RESPONSIBILITY, TO ME,
TO TELL THE TRUTH AND TO

00:02:11.720 --> 00:02:16.930
WRITE HISTORY THE WAY THAT IT WAS
AND HOW IT CONNECTS US TO TODAY

00:02:16.930 --> 00:02:19.959
AND WHAT WE SEE GOING ON IN
THE WORLD TODAY.

00:02:19.959 --> 00:02:26.040
AND YEAH, I’M JUST, I HAVE NO WORDS,
I’M JUST SO, SO, SO HAPPY AND GRATEFUL

00:02:26.040 --> 00:02:29.069
AND YEAH, KNOWLEDGE IS POWER.

00:02:29.069 --> 00:02:32.180
MUSIC IS POWER.

00:02:32.180 --> 00:02:33.539
AND AS LONG AS 
I’M STANDING,

00:02:33.539 --> 00:02:34.800
 I’M ALWAYS GOING
TO FIGHT FOR US.

00:02:34.800 --> 00:02:36.909
I’M ALWAYS GOING TO FIGHT FOR
MY PEOPLE AND FIGHT FOR

00:02:36.909 --> 00:02:38.800
WHAT’S RIGHT, AND I THINK THAT’S
WHAT MUSIC DOES.

00:02:38.800 --> 00:02:40.000
AND THAT’S WHAT
STORYTELLING DOES.

00:02:40.000 --> 00:02:41.140
SO THANK YOU SO MUCH.

00:02:41.140 --> 00:02:42.072
THANK YOU.

